 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Totally normal. Many people are, and bike being smaller stop traffic as easily as car does. Short commutes are fine, but for commuting you need plan B for when the road is blocked. Walk part of it, use a bridge or street that stays open longer. It is. The key is always having a backup plan. Check traffic before heading out, and don't start when you' expect to be at work on a busy commute. Then stick a friend with knowledge of your route as your backup. If something stops you message them first.",
